# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# RoyCSS — Root .env.example (Next.js app)
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The Next.js app (port 3000) talks to the Express backend (port 4000)
# via the gateway, so it needs NO API keys directly — all secrets live
# in `backend/.env` and are read server-side by the backend.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` ONLY if you need to override the defaults
# below for local development. Never commit a populated .env file.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Next.js Runtime ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set automatically by `next dev` / `next build && next start`.
# Override here ONLY for advanced scenarios.
# NODE_ENV=development

# ─── Backend URL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public base URL of the Express backend, used for any client-side
# deep links to API docs. Defaults to the same-origin /api proxy.
# BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:4000
